From 1797c0fb4e7bf00c21ce20a741e40bd6c52e673a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:46:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] prefill: STRATA_HANDOFF_PIPE=P hands a layer split's
 chunk on in P pieces, gated by events, on a persistent thread

A layer split hands each prompt chunk's rows (21 MB per 512 tokens) to the next card through a pinned
host buffer: one D2H, a host stream sync, a new std::async thread, then one H2D before the next stage's
first kernel.  The 3090s here have no P2P (topo: CNS) and cudaMemcpyPeerAsync is driver-staged and
slower (3.4 ms vs 3.2 ms for D2H + H2D), so the copy stays on the host route; nsys showed 3.8-4.0 ms per
512-row hop, of which ~1-1.4 ms was the thread start alone.

With STRATA_HANDOFF_PIPE=P (2..16, opt-in; unset = unchanged):
- the sending stage records an event when its chunk's work is done and one after each of P row-piece
  downloads into the same pinned buffer, and waits on the host only for the first (on_stage_chunk's
  checkpoint parts and the error check need the state, not the copy);
- the next stage waits on the GPU for each piece's event (cross-device cudaStreamWaitEvent) before that
  piece's upload, so its uploads overlap the remaining downloads (separate PCIe links); a smaller
  receiving chunk waits for every piece, then copies as before;
- the next stage's chunks run on one worker thread per sending stage, started and pinned once, whose
  packaged_task futures carry the same results and exceptions as std::async's (it clears the CUDA error
  state after each job, as a thread's end did).  STRATA_HANDOFF_PIPE_WORKER=0 keeps std::async (A/B).

Same bytes in the same rows before the next stage's first kernel: exact.  No device memory (events only,
the existing two pinned buffers per stage).  Measured (T16-143l5, P=8): 512-row hops 3.8-4.0 -> 1.85-1.89
ms, 143-row hops 1.6 -> 1.0 ms; reads 1.2K about -1.5 %, 150 about -1 %, 9K (agent, --kv-resident) -3 %;
decode rows/s unchanged.  batch_test16/32 (greedy and temperature 0.7), batch_interleave_test and
batch_overlap_test (+ the stage fault arm) byte-/token-identical to the reference dumps; an agent-config
run with checkpoint parts byte-identical to the reference binary.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
